<!--
  BlockML Core — fix expression errors task

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.task.FixExpressionErrors
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:diag="org.blockml.bml.diagnostic"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.task">

  <name>FixExpressionErrors</name>
  <type>task:FixExpressionErrors</type>
  <baseType>core:TaskGuide</baseType>
  <is>A how-to for fixing expression errors</is>

  <summary>Resolve ${ } and &lt;$ $&gt; expression diagnostics — syntax, unknown refs, type/payload
    mismatches, linking, and model context.</summary>

  <keywords>expression, BML_EXPR_SYNTAX_ERROR, bean, built-in, embedded</keywords>

  <documentation>
    Procedure when an expression-related BML_EXPR_* (or embed) diagnostic is reported:
    1. Confirm host context — member ${ } vs implementation &lt;$ $&gt; (doc:EmbeddedExpressions).
    2. Syntax errors — check delimiters, quotes, operators; embeds must not nest &lt;$ $&gt;.
    3. Unknown property — verify member exists in scope; StructType fields by name only (not [0]).
    4. Unknown bean / builtin — declare bml:bean Aggregation or use a V1 #built-in.
    5. Type / payload mismatch — align expression result with member type; map call args via
       FunctionMapping (doc:FunctionMappingModel).
    6. Linking (@bean.capa without parens) — source Outbound, target Inbound, compatible payloads.
    7. Relative @model: — ensure a parent Aggregation established binding context.
    8. V1 — avoid deferred @bean execution / model / linking features until implemented.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:Expressions" relation="TaskStep">
      Step 1 — ${ } language, scope, V1 support.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:EmbeddedExpressions" relation="TaskStep">
      Step 2 — implementation embeds and delimiter rules.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:FunctionMappingModel" relation="TaskStep">
      Step 3 — call argument mapping diagnostics.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:BmlDirectives" relation="TaskStep">
      Step 4 — each/with variable scopes.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_EXPR_SYNTAX_ERROR" relation="SeeAlso">
      Parse failure diagnostic.
    </see>
    <see type="diag:BML_EXPR_UNKNOWN_PROPERTY" relation="SeeAlso">
      Unknown property / invalid struct index access.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
